  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The United States House of Representatives successfully blocked an effort to impeach Secretary of Defense Pete Hegseth. The impeachment motion was introduced by Republican Congressman Thomas Massie, who alleged that the Defense Secretary knowingly carried out unlawful orders associated with the ongoing war in Iran. Had the measure proceeded, Hegseth would have become the first US defense secretary to face impeachment. Following the vote, President Donald Trump publicly supported the outcome, characterizing Hegseth as a dedicated public servant. While the immediate effort has been halted by the Republican-controlled House, reports indicate that the path remains open for potential future challenges from opponents. The Secretary of Defense previously dismissed the accusations against him, describing the impeachment attempt as a political maneuver or farce aimed at his critics of the administration.",
